seccomp: replace epoll_create when the policy rejects it

Android's app seccomp policy on x86_64 (emulators, Waydroid) rejects the legacy
epoll_create, which arm64 never had. Flutter's Linux embedder creates its
message loop with epoll_create(1), so Flutter apps such as LocalSend aborted with
"Check failed: epoll_fd_.is_valid()". epoll_wait is already replaced below.

--- a/src/tracee/seccomp.c	2026-10-28 12:50:59.891411163 +0530
+++ b/src/tracee/seccomp.c	2026-10-28 12:52:29.333078130 +0530
@@ -197,6 +197,14 @@
 		restart_syscall_after_seccomp(tracee);
 		break;
 
+	case PR_epoll_create:
+		/* Android's app policy on x86_64 rejects the legacy call, which
+		 * Flutter's Linux embedder makes; its size argument is unused.  */
+		set_sysnum(tracee, PR_epoll_create1);
+		poke_reg(tracee, SYSARG_1, 0);
+		restart_syscall_after_seccomp(tracee);
+		break;
+
 	case PR_setgroups:
 	case PR_setgroups32:
 		set_result_after_seccomp(tracee, 0);
